## Problem classes

### `JNI and libzt both loaded fighting UDP`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Bind fail on 9993/9994, or dual hello | Both nodes started | Orchestrator exclusive start; phase-2 spike; isolated process only as last resort (still one identity opener) |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `LAN proxy`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Other devices can use the phone as proxy | Bound `0.0.0.0` | `InetSocketAddress("127.0.0.1", 0)` |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `Ephemeral bind port`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| UI/logs show port `0` after start | Archive returned ctor arg, not kernel-assigned port | After `bind`, expose `boundPort = serverSocket.localPort`; persist for system-proxy write (T06) |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `Route priority tie-break`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Wrong ZT net chosen when two nets share same prefix length | Archive LPM had no tie-break | In `resolveIpString`, equal `prefixLength` → lower `routePriority` wins |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `Proxy start while VPN up`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Dual stack / UDP fight / refused start | JNI node still running | Refuse proxy start when VPN `isRunning`; `EXTRA_FORCE_DEBUG` only for dev JNI→libzt spike |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->
